alue "continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447531} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1109bc7-547a-500f-b40b-e4d37aec3c09" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447621}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d5d0172c-6e34-5d1d-9e31-e326cbe0c123" :question/math-academy-id "q-341195" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $4$-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=-4{x}^{2}+1$ defined on $[-2,2).$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of the Fourier series of the $4$-periodic extension of $G(x)=-8x$ from the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$\n\nThe Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n-4{x}^{2}+1∼-\\frac{13}{3}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{64(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is \n{{field-2}}\nand\n{{field-3}}\non $R,$ we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\n-8x∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-4}}\\cdot {{field-5}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $F(x)$ is an even function. So, the Fourier series of its $2L$-periodic extension has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=2$ and we are already given the coefficients ${a}_{0}$ and ${a}_{n}$ for $n\\ge 1.$ Thus, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼-\\frac{13}{3}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{64(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that \n\n- the function $F$ is continuously differentiable on $(-2,2),$\n\n- continuous on $[-2,2),$ and\n\n- satisfies $F(-2)=F(2),$ if we extend the value at $x=2$ using the formula $F(x)=-4{x}^{2}+1.$\n\nTherefore, the $4$-periodic extension $f$ is $\\text{continuous}$ and $\\text{piecewise smooth}$ on $R,$ so we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-4{x}^{2}+1) & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{13}{3})+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{64(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})) \\\\ -8x & ∼0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{64(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\cdot (-\\frac{n\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})) \\\\ -8x & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{-32(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}) \\\\ -8x & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{32(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222036 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221450 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2e37d37-007c-569b-a44c-cb6a9d075371" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Fourier Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ee7e427-46c3-5aed-9b19-381c6b43ae67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{nx}{\\pi })" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447524} {:answer/id #uuid "84d02c9f-09db-5f84-8395-ecb31c424496" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447546} {:answer/id #uuid "d0cf8966-1bef-51d6-8f2d-fa9d3c63371e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{nx}{\\pi })" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447577} {:answer/id #uuid "d80d207a-d991-5083-a552-3b5c5c3785d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447582}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d80d207a-d991-5083-a552-3b5c5c3785d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447582} :