"6552293c-ef9b-5d65-a476-a37433b05e66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14(-1)^{n+1}}{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447532} :answer-field/id #uuid "f55713f6-e85d-551a-86cb-466027170f89" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447626}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b5d5810a-d922-539c-8f81-743a41d8a84a" :question/math-academy-id "q-343315" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=\\frac{7}{2}{x}^{2}+3$ defined on $[-\\pi ,\\pi ).$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of the Fourier series of the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $G(x)=7x$ from the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$\n\nThe Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{2}{x}^{2}+3∼3+\\frac{7{\\pi }^{2}}{6}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{14(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}}{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is \n{{field-2}}\nand\n{{field-3}}\non $R,$ we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\n7x∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-4}}\\cdot {{field-5}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $F(x)$ is an even function. So, the Fourier series of its $2L$-periodic extension has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=\\pi $ and we are already given the coefficients ${a}_{0}$ and ${a}_{n}$ for $n\\ge 1.$ Thus, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼3+\\frac{7{\\pi }^{2}}{6}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{14(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that \n\n- the function $F$ is continuously differentiable on $(-\\pi ,\\pi ),$\n\n- continuous on $[-\\pi ,\\pi ),$ and\n\n- satisfies $F(-\\pi )=F(\\pi ),$ if we extend the value at $x=\\pi $ using the formula $F(x)=\\frac{7}{2}{x}^{2}+3.$\n\nTherefore, the $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f$ is $\\text{continuous}$ and $\\text{piecewise smooth}$ on $R,$ so we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{7}{2}{x}^{2}+3) & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3+\\frac{7{\\pi }^{2}}{6})+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{14(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)) \\\\ 7x & ∼0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{14(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}}\\cdot (-n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)) \\\\ 7x & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{-14(-1)^{n}}{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx) \\\\ 7x & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{14(-1)^{n+1}}{n}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317389 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221451 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c1e01d04-6c13-52eb-a4b6-ad9a5cde8134" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Fourier Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30654a61-bca2-5d45-8dfd-6666c2232131" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315391} {:answer/id #uuid "481d3ffb-b826-5c26-abd5-24a0975fb43c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315535} {:answer/id #uuid "57b480dc-e5e7-550b-882b-cb01488fd141" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315626} {:answer/id #uuid "5a702db4-464c-52c5-ae25-6568483b6169" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315632}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30654a61-bca2-5d45-8dfd-6666c2232131" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315391} :answer-field/id #uuid "118aaf33-e092-57ae-ad75-e10e6a5a7996" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316589} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0369724f-0d94-5066-8c6d-06eee2316ce0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "odd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315136} {:answer/id #uuid "2272ec4e-6d60-5d4a-8e26-dfa44c7f7097" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "piecewise continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315308} {:answer/id #uuid "7c4d0ed2-69a5-5df4-bdc3-0fc96726b52a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "even" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315808} {:answer/id #uuid "c1c001ea-6af4-548a-b0b9-b3d01b3ebf83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "periodic" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316206}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2272ec4e-6d60-5d4a-8e26-dfa44c7f7097" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "piecewise continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315308} :answer-field/id #uuid "969b70b1-fcf1-530b-977f-41d3ceacc8b2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316892} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "437a1983-ea9c-5b88-8dc2-8237185da01b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315510} {:answer/id #uuid "4604ac7b-ebad-50c4-be31-0f256f65d144" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315523} {:answer/id #uuid "5